      "property": "Stroke construction: 1-pixel caps, 3-pixel runs, 5-pixel vertex row (about 2.1 px perpendicular)",
      "observed": "run lengths 1, 3, 5",
      "authority": "fixture property; expert acceptance",
      "source": "none; the request imposed no stroke width",
      "reasoning": "A 1-px diagonal at 16x16 breaks up on a dark panel at 1x; 3-px runs give an effective 2-px stroke that survives 1x and becomes a solid 6-device-pixel stroke at 3x. Pointed caps keep the mark from looking like a blunt bar and are consistent with the Start triangle's sharp vertices."
    },
    {
      "property": "Placement bbox [3,4,14,13], margins L3 R2 T4 B3",
      "observed": "bbox centre (8.5, 8.5) versus cell centre (8, 8)",
      "authority": "fixture property; expert acceptance",
      "source": "none",
      "reasoning": "An 11x9 figure cannot be exactly centred on a 16x16 grid; the half-pixel bias right and down is the normal rounding choice. All margins are at least 2 px so the 3x nearest view has no edge contact, and the occupied region (about 12x10 centred) is a usable shared envelope for Working, Retry and Paused."
    },
    {
      "property": "Uniform 1:1 stair-step rhythm",
      "observed": "no run-length anomalies",
      "authority": "fixture property; expert judgment (edge-rhythm)",
      "source": "none",
      "reasoning": "Even steps are why the 3x view looks deliberate rather than jagged. A 45-degree stroke is the one diagonal angle that needs no anti-aliasing to look clean, which also keeps alpha binary."
    },
    {
      "property": "Binary alpha",
      "observed": "alpha only 0 and 255",
      "authority": "fixture property; brief and plan permit partial alpha",
      "source": "BRIEF.md line 3 does not restrict alpha; plan contract alpha 'full'",
      "reasoning": "Binary alpha is the simplest contract for nearest-neighbour display and avoids premultiplication questions in the unknown renderer. It is accepted, not required."
    },
    {
      "property": "No outline, no plate or badge behind the mark",
      "observed": "single component, no secondary colour",
      "authority": "fixture property; expert acceptance",
      "source": "none",
      "reasoning": "On a fixed dark panel the light fill already separates from the background (observed ratio about 7.4:1); an outline would spend 2 of 16 pixels of budget and a plate would compete with the plate-less Start triangle. If the family is ever shown on light or busy backgrounds this decision should be revisited (silhouette-readability)."
    },
    {
      "property": "Single connected component",
      "observed": "1 component (4- and 8-connected)",
      "authority": "measurement only",
      "source": "pixl_asset_check",
      "reasoning": "A count is not a quality verdict; here it simply confirms the two arms are joined, which the check-mark reading depends on."
    }
  ],
  "verdict_agreement": {
    "statement": "The six retained verdicts (ready.delivery.review.verdict.0-5, reviewer actor, all pass) are not re-scored or superseded here. My own current viewing of the three retained views and the decoded PNG agrees with each pass.",
    "per_criterion": {
      "geometry": "agree: 16x16, one frame",
      "transparent-background": "agree: exterior alpha 0, no matte or fringe",
      "ready-meaning": "agree: clear check, unequal arms, not a triangle, bars, loop or cross",
      "readability-1x-3x": "agree: readable at both scales on #172336",
      "cool-blue-accent": "agree: fill equals the Start accent",
      "sample-pixel-craft": "agree as a scoped expert judgment: crisp clusters, even steps, no strays; the treatment is extensible"
    }
  },
  "family_guidance_proposals": {
    "status": "specialist proposals only; family/style adoption and any generation are separate future work with their own authorization",
    "shared_recipe": "Flat single-tone fills, effective 2-px stroke (3-pixel runs on diagonals, 2-pixel runs on orthogonals), 45-degree or orthogonal strokes with uniform step rhythm, pointed 1-px caps where a stroke ends, no outline or plate, binary alpha, content inside roughly columns 3-13 and rows 3-13 of the 16x16 cell.",
    "working": {
      "consumer_facts": "src/queue-view.ts line 4: assets/working.png, frames 4; line 9: frameMs 100, nearest, scale 3. BRIEF.md line 3: four horizontal frames, 100 ms, must communicate activity without looking like success.",
      "proposal": "One 64x16 horizontal strip of four 16x16 frames (frame i at columns 16i..16i+15), uniform 100 ms, looping total 400 ms. Motif: a partial ring or three orbiting dots in the same #70b9ed stroke weight that rotates a quarter turn per frame so the silhouette changes every frame. Rule to test, not a requirement: no single frame may contain a two-arm check-like stroke, and no frame should be mistakable for Ready when the loop is stopped. Per state-driven-pixel-ui the loop should play only while state is running."
    },
    "retry": {
      "consumer_facts": "src/queue-view.ts line 7: assets/error-retry.png, frames 1. BRIEF.md line 3: error/retry distinguishable without colour alone; line 7: path moved, purpose unchanged.",
      "proposal": "Static circular arrow or an X-with-arrow form whose shape alone differs from the check; grayscale comparison at 1x and 3x against Ready is the test. A warmer accent may be added but may not be the only cue."
    },
    "paused": {
      "consumer_facts": "src/queue-view.ts line 5: assets/paused.png, frames 1. BRIEF.md line 7: distinguishable from activity, completion and retry without colour alone.",
      "proposal": "Two vertical 2-px bars with a 2-px gap, same height envelope as the check (rows 4-12), flat #70b9ed. Form is orthogonal where Ready is diagonal and Working is rotational, so grayscale distinction is carried by geometry."
    },
    "baseline_suitability": "The delivered Ready is suitable as the family style baseline (proposal). Its rules are few and transferable: one tone, one stroke weight, even steps, no decoration. Risk to record: a single flat tone leaves no shading vocabulary, so if the owner later wants depth or highlights the whole family would change together. Adoption remains the caller/owner decision and should be source-bound to assets/ready-confirmed.png sha256 fc5e43ae... when made."
  },
  "limits": [
    "No graphical renderer was available; nearest sampling, alpha compositing and full/compact display are unverified beyond source-module execution.",
    "Light or busy background readability was not tested because the consumer declares only #172336.",
    "The image is a controlled evaluator fixture; nothing here measures live provider behaviour.",
    "This assessment is specialist judgment; the independent caller comparison is pending."
  ]
}

